\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}Class\nobreakspace  {}A sensitivity. Cumulative number of independent systems whose best window reaches a given EIRP, for $P_{90}^{\rm  sel}$, the power passing the complete automated selection (solid), and for $P_{90}$, which reaches the trigger only (dashed). The shaded band is the systematic budget: the calibration bracket $\times 0.64$--$\times 1.04$, plus the one-sided $+20$ per cent atmospheric-decorrelation bias, which is why it is asymmetric. \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}The temporal selection function: systems grouped by the longest separation between their searched epochs, an independent epoch being defined as a separation of more than 1{} day. \textbf  {For the 27{} systems with a single block and the 13{} whose blocks all fall within one day --- left of the dashed line --- independent confirmation was not possible at all}, whatever the sensitivity in panel\nobreakspace  {}(a). Recurrence over years can be tested for 23{} systems.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:classasens}{{4}{8}{\emph {(a)}~Class~A sensitivity. Cumulative number of independent systems whose best window reaches a given EIRP, for $P_{90}^{\rm sel}$, the power passing the complete automated selection (solid), and for $P_{90}$, which reaches the trigger only (dashed). The shaded band is the systematic budget: the calibration bracket $\times \SelTransFineLo $--$\times \SelTransFineHi $, plus the one-sided $+\BudDecorHi $ per cent atmospheric-decorrelation bias, which is why it is asymmetric. \emph {(b)}~The temporal selection function: systems grouped by the longest separation between their searched epochs, an independent epoch being defined as a separation of more than \EpSep {} day. \textbf {For the \EpOne {} systems with a single block and the \EpSameDay {} whose blocks all fall within one day --- left of the dashed line --- independent confirmation was not possible at all}, whatever the sensitivity in panel~(a). Recurrence over years can be tested for \EpYears {} systems}{figure.4}{}}
