\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The chain that disposes of a threshold crossing, with the number surviving each step, and the drift-following visibility fit reported beside it rather than within it. Every count is read from the ledger, so the figure and Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:ledger} cannot disagree. The fit sits outside the column because it is evaluated at the position and in the cell where the search already found an excess, and because its twelve controls resolve a rank of 1/13{} (\S  \ref  {sec:vistest}); it confirms the search rather than testing it independently.}}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:chain}{{5}{12}{The chain that disposes of a threshold crossing, with the number surviving each step, and the drift-following visibility fit reported beside it rather than within it. Every count is read from the ledger, so the figure and Table~\ref {tab:ledger} cannot disagree. The fit sits outside the column because it is evaluated at the position and in the cell where the search already found an excess, and because its twelve controls resolve a rank of \EpVisRankRes {} (\S \ref {sec:vistest}); it confirms the search rather than testing it independently}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The ledger in counts, each against chance. The line-mask expectation is the mask's 4.1{} per cent occupancy of the searched band times the 56{} crossings; the localisation expectations are the measured false-alarm rate of the full criterion on 577{} event-free control samples --- 0.69{} and 0.17{} per cent under the two epochs, both inside the 1{} per cent ceiling fixed before the campaign --- times the number fitted. The Re/$\sigma \ge 4$ clause alone fires at 3.29{} and 2.77{} per cent, so the imaginary-part clause is carrying the criterion.}}{12}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ledgersum}{{4}{12}{The ledger in counts, each against chance. The line-mask expectation is the mask's \LgMaskOccPct {} per cent occupancy of the searched band times the \LgNCross {} crossings; the localisation expectations are the measured false-alarm rate of the full criterion on \LgFaNCor {} event-free control samples --- \LgFaPctCom {} and \LgFaPctCor {} per cent under the two epochs, both inside the \LgFaCeilPct {} per cent ceiling fixed before the campaign --- times the number fitted. The Re/$\sigma \ge \LgReMin $ clause alone fires at \LgFaPctReCom {} and \LgFaPctReCor {} per cent, so the imaginary-part clause is carrying the criterion}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The duty-cycle selection function, measured. Recovery probability against transmitter power, in units of $P_{90}$, and duty cycle $f_{\rm  dwell}$, from 3\,888{} injection trials. The abscissa is in units of $P_{90}$, the measured trigger completeness of \S  \ref  {sec:pninetysel}, which for Class\nobreakspace  {}A is $\times 3.0$ the nominal trigger power. Recovery at $f_{\rm  dwell}=0.10$ is 71{} per cent for the fine class and 83{} for the coarse, rising to 91{} and 100{} at $f_{\rm  dwell}=0.25$ (Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:inject}). The dwell injections are zero-drift, so this selection function is measured for a stationary carrier and transferred to the drifting primary experiment; the joint drifting-and-intermittent cell of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:classcomp} remains unmeasured.}}{13}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dwellsel}{{6}{13}{The duty-cycle selection function, measured. Recovery probability against transmitter power, in units of $P_{90}$, and duty cycle $f_{\rm dwell}$, from \NDwellTrials {} injection trials. The abscissa is in units of $P_{90}$, the measured trigger completeness of \S \ref {sec:pninetysel}, which for Class~A is $\times \SelPNinetyTrigFine $ the nominal trigger power. Recovery at $f_{\rm dwell}=0.10$ is \DwellFineT {} per cent for the fine class and \DwellCoarseT {} for the coarse, rising to \DwellFineQ {} and \DwellCoarseQ {} at $f_{\rm dwell}=0.25$ (Appendix~\ref {app:inject}). The dwell injections are zero-drift, so this selection function is measured for a stationary carrier and transferred to the drifting primary experiment; the joint drifting-and-intermittent cell of Table~\ref {tab:classcomp} remains unmeasured}{figure.6}{}}
