\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces The CP$-$72\nobreakspace  {}2713 repeat test, both blocks side by side, separating ``not detected again'' from ``a persistent signal of the original strength would have been recovered''. The repeat block is the deeper of the two, matches the first in tuning, channelisation and integration, and its frequency axis registers to a fifth of a channel. A source at the first block's flux would have returned $T_\star =6.21$ there; the measured value is 4.70. Intermittent emission is not excluded by this test, and no statement here assumes otherwise.}}{36}{table.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cprepeat}{{23}{36}{The CP$-$72~2713 repeat test, both blocks side by side, separating ``not detected again'' from ``a persistent signal of the original strength would have been recovered''. The repeat block is the deeper of the two, matches the first in tuning, channelisation and integration, and its frequency axis registers to a fifth of a channel. A source at the first block's flux would have returned $T_\star =\CpRecExpT $ there; the measured value is \CpTstarTwo . Intermittent emission is not excluded by this test, and no statement here assumes otherwise}{table.23}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces The injection campaign resolved by configuration. $P_{50}$ and $P_{90}$ are the injected amplitudes, in units of the local noise, at which half and nine-tenths of trials are recovered. No axis shows a deficit large enough to move the quoted threshold outside the window-to-window bracket of $\times 0.48$--$\times 1.35$; the sub-channel-phase rows are mean response factors, not recovery amplitudes, and are the reason the threshold carries a response correction.}}{36}{table.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:driftstrata}{{24}{36}{The injection campaign resolved by configuration. $P_{50}$ and $P_{90}$ are the injected amplitudes, in units of the local noise, at which half and nine-tenths of trials are recovered. No axis shows a deficit large enough to move the quoted threshold outside the window-to-window bracket of $\times \StratTransferNineLo $--$\times \StratTransferNineHi $; the sub-channel-phase rows are mean response factors, not recovery amplitudes, and are the reason the threshold carries a response correction}{table.24}{}}
