\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}The drift-following visibility fit for every crossing that could be fitted, in units of the measurement uncertainty: the real part of the visibility phase-rotated to the stellar position against its imaginary part. Open symbols are the committed reference epoch, filled the adopted one, joined for each crossing. Emission centred on the star makes the real part positive and significant and leaves the imaginary part near zero; emission displaced from the phase centre does not. Grey points are the control positions and control frequencies of the same fits, which carry no event by construction and show the null. The shaded region is the localisation criterion, fixed and committed at \texttt  {edfcc0d3d7db}{} before any of these fits was run. \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}The same verdicts against $|D|$, the channel displacement between the two epochs: every crossing whose verdict moves does so above about one channel, and none moves below 0.25, which is where the injection campaign says the two conventions are the same experiment.}}{41}{figure.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ledgervis}{{15}{41}{\emph {(a)}~The drift-following visibility fit for every crossing that could be fitted, in units of the measurement uncertainty: the real part of the visibility phase-rotated to the stellar position against its imaginary part. Open symbols are the committed reference epoch, filled the adopted one, joined for each crossing. Emission centred on the star makes the real part positive and significant and leaves the imaginary part near zero; emission displaced from the phase centre does not. Grey points are the control positions and control frequencies of the same fits, which carry no event by construction and show the null. The shaded region is the localisation criterion, fixed and committed at \LgCommit {} before any of these fits was run. \emph {(b)}~The same verdicts against $|D|$, the channel displacement between the two epochs: every crossing whose verdict moves does so above about one channel, and none moves below \LgDSame , which is where the injection campaign says the two conventions are the same experiment}{figure.15}{}}
